This directory is the code broker's workspace: one checkout per household
member, under the member's own subdirectory.

The broker refuses to clone into a directory that does not carry this file,
under the name `.nanobot-code-workspace`. Its absence means CODE_WORKSPACE_DIR
points somewhere nobody intended -- a home directory, or a mount that did not
appear -- and cloning into that is worse than refusing.

Upstream's build-multiuser.sh wrote it. This package does not ship that script,
so nothing wrote it at all and the broker refused every request while reporting
itself healthy; the deploy seeds it from here now.
